---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="ArkheionX Docs"
  description="Official ArkheionX documentation for local-first smart contract security review workflows."
>
  <main class="docs-home">
    <section class="docs-hero">
      <p class="docs-kicker">Documentation</p>
      <h1>Start with the review map.</h1>
      <p>
        ArkheionX helps security teams turn a Solidity or Foundry repository into structured
        review context: contracts, roles, value paths, assumptions, test gaps, evidence, fixture
        benchmarks, and snapshot drift.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-start-grid">
      <a href="/docs/getting-started">
        <span>01</span>
        <h2>Getting started</h2>
        <p>Understand what ArkheionX is, who it is for, and what to expect.</p>
      </a>

      <a href="/docs/installation">
        <span>02</span>
        <h2>Installation</h2>
        <p>Install from source, inspect the installer, update, and uninstall.</p>
      </a>

      <a href="/docs/quickstart">
        <span>03</span>
        <h2>Quickstart</h2>
        <p>Run the first local commands and confirm the tool is available.</p>
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
      <div>
        <p class="docs-kicker">Core concepts</p>
        <h2>The vocabulary of a review map.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="docs-concept-grid">
        <a href="/docs/concepts">
          <strong>Protocol surface</strong>
          <p>The parts of a codebase that matter for review: actors, permissions, value paths, and assumptions.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/fixture-harness">
          <strong>Fixture harness</strong>
          <p>Local/static benchmark shapes for checking deterministic output and drift.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/determinism">
          <strong>Determinism</strong>
          <p>Stable IDs, JSON-safe outputs, source fingerprints, and reproducible snapshots.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/safety-model">
          <strong>Safety model</strong>
          <p>What ArkheionX does not do: no automatic vulnerability confirmation or audit replacement.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
      <div>
        <p class="docs-kicker">Workflow</p>
        <h2>Use ArkheionX as review infrastructure.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="docs-workflow">
        <article>
          <span>1</span>
          <h3>Install locally</h3>
          <p>Use the source installer or a manual GitHub checkout.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>2</span>
          <h3>Check the environment</h3>
          <p>Run version and doctor commands before reviewing a codebase.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>3</span>
          <h3>Build context</h3>
          <p>Use ArkheionX outputs to organize assumptions, evidence, and gaps.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>4</span>
          <h3>Review manually</h3>
          <p>The tool supports human review. It does not make the final security judgment.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
      <div>
        <p class="docs-kicker">Workflows &amp; release</p>
        <h2>How it works, and how teams use it.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="docs-concept-grid">
        <a href="/docs/how-it-works">
          <strong>How it works</strong>
          <p>The review-map pipeline: from a local repo to value paths, assumptions, test gaps, and proof directions.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/bug-bounty">
          <strong>Bug bounty</strong>
          <p>A safe triage and hypothesis workbench. No exploits, no submission, human review required.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/pre-audit">
          <strong>Pre-audit</strong>
          <p>Map value paths, close test gaps, and hand a reviewer a clearer surface before an audit.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/v4">
          <strong>V4 release</strong>
          <p>What V4 stabilizes, what stays experimental, and the known limitations.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/research-memory">
          <strong>Research memory (v4.1)</strong>
          <p>AI-assisted review: an agent brief, a hypothesis log, and a case-study generator. Hypotheses are prompts, not findings.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/v5">
          <strong>Blind Spot Intelligence (v5)</strong>
          <p>Prioritize high-impact surfaces with weak review evidence: blind-spots, criticality-map, counterfactuals. Not severity, not bug claims.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/research-pack">
          <strong>Research pack (v5)</strong>
          <p>Bundle blind spots, criticality, counterfactuals, an agent brief, and an evidence log into one local, vendor-agnostic pack.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section docs-section--links">
      <a href="/docs/review-workflow">Review workflow</a>
      <a href="/docs/cli-reference">CLI reference</a>
      <a href="/docs/troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a>
      <a href="/docs/faq">FAQ</a>
      <a href="/arkheionx-v4-technical-paper.pdf">Technical paper</a>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
